### V-E Stable Transcriptomic Signatures Recover Immune and Host-Defense Biology

PSI-ranked genes were also subjected to Gene Ontology and KEGG enrichment analysis to determine whether highly stable transcriptomic features corresponded to established sepsis pathophysiology mechanisms. Representative enriched Gene Ontology biological-process terms and KEGG pathways are summarized in Table IV.
pp-value (FDR). Genes: number of stable features annotated to the term; Fold Enr.: fold enrichment over the genomic background. 
ID | Term | Genes | Fold Enr. | FDR (qq)
...
Gene Ontology (Biological Process) 
GO:0006959 | humoral immune response | 23 | 7.8 | 2.3×10−112.3\times 10^{-11} 
GO:0009617 | response to bacterium | 39 | 4.1 | 3.7×10−113.7\times 10^{-11} 
GO:0042742 | defense response to bacterium | 24 | 5.9 | 1.7×10−91.7\times 10^{-9} 
GO:0019730 | antimicrobial humoral response | 14 | 9.7 | 4.3×10−84.3\times 10^{-8} 
GO:0007159 | leukocyte cell-cell adhesion | 30 | 3.5 | 8.3×10−78.3\times 10^{-7} 
GO:0006954 | inflammatory response | 40 | 2.7 | 1.9×10−61.9\times 10^{-6} 
KEGG Pathways 
hsa05150 | Staphylococcus aureus infection | 16 | 9.7 | 3.2×10−103.2\times 10^{-10} 
hsa04145 | Phagocytosis | 30 | 4.2 | 1.1×10−91.1\times 10^{-9} 
hsa04640 | Hematopoietic cell lineage | 13 | 5.3 | 3.9×10−53.9\times 10^{-5} 
hsa05140 | Leishmaniasis | 11 | 5.1 | 2.2×10−42.2\times 10^{-4} 

Immune and host-defense processes were the highest ranking enrichment terms. Representative examples include antibacterial responses, antimicrobial humoral immunity, leukocyte activation, inflammatory signaling and antigen presentation. These medical themes support the biological plausibility of the stable transcriptomic signals identified by PSI and are consistent and aligned with dysregulated host immune response that characterizes sepsis.

